From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mempage4k <mempage4k@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wgpu-hal: Metal occlusion queries reset before reuse

reset_queries did nothing on Metal, but a render pass writes an
occlusion query's slot in the visibility result buffer only when a draw
runs while the query is active. A query begun and ended with no draw in
between (a D3D11 query that spans two render passes has such a part in
the first) then read whatever the slot's last use had left there.

A game that measures the sun's visibility with occlusion queries reused
its slots every few hundred frames: the sun's query read tens of
thousands of samples (another query's) with no sky on screen, and the
lens flare showed through walls and floors.

reset_queries now zeroes the queries' slots with a blit, as Vulkan's
vkCmdResetQueryPool does; wgpu-core records it before the render pass.
---
diff --git a/src/metal/command.rs b/src/metal/command.rs
index 46ee564..0d0d2ba 100644
--- a/src/metal/command.rs
+++ b/src/metal/command.rs
@@ -903,7 +903,21 @@ impl crate::CommandEncoder for super::CommandEncoder {
         };
     }
 
-    unsafe fn reset_queries(&mut self, _set: &super::QuerySet, _range: Range<u32>) {}
+    unsafe fn reset_queries(&mut self, set: &super::QuerySet, range: Range<u32>) {
+        // A render pass writes an occlusion query's result only if a draw
+        // runs while the query is active: zeroed here, a query begun and
+        // ended with no draw between reads 0, not what the slot's last use
+        // left there.
+        if let wgt::QueryType::Occlusion = set.ty {
+            let size = crate::QUERY_SIZE as usize;
+            let encoder = self.enter_blit();
+            encoder.fillBuffer_range_value(
+                &set.raw_buffer,
+                NSRange::new(range.start as usize * size, (range.end - range.start) as usize * size),
+                0,
+            );
+        }
+    }
 
     unsafe fn copy_query_results(
         &mut self,
